From bee340efa022ef3867489e264eae2f73654efc73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: airidosas252 <airidaslideikis@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:29:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 03/20] ir3, tu: Emulate 32-wide subgroups on A8XX

A8XX only runs 64-wide waves, but D3D12 shaders can require
[WaveSize(32)], which vkd3d-proton maps to requiredSubgroupSize = 32.
Advertise minSubgroupSize = 32 and lower such shaders in one of two ways:

 - narrow mode: workgroups of at most 32 invocations run as one
   half-populated wave. No code changes are needed.
 - split mode: each 64-lane wave runs two virtual 32-lane subgroups.
   The API-level NIR goes through nir_lower_subgroups with
   subgroup_size = 32. The residue is then translated to physical
   operations: lane & 31, id = 2 * hw_id + (lane >> 5), half ballots,
   reductions and scans with logical-lane guards. The physical compiler
   subgroup stays 64.

Shaders without a required size are unchanged.

VK-CTS on Adreno 840 (KGSL), dEQP-VK.subgroups.*, before -> after:
  size_control       48 / 0 / 15 -> 36 / 0 / 27 (graphics-stage
                     required_subgroup_size_{min,max} no longer advertised)
  ballot_broadcast  747 / 0 / 5370 -> 888 / 0 / 5229 (+141 requiredsubgroupsize32)
  basic, builtin_var, ballot, ballot_other, vote, quad, shuffle, clustered,
  arithmetic: identical results before and after
  subgroups.size_control.mesh.* 10/10, subgroups.basic.mesh.* 24/24
  dEQP-VK.compute.pipeline.basic.*               75 pass, 0 fail, 7 not supported
Full dEQP-VK.subgroups.* (with the mesh flags): 20115 pass, 1 fail, 28589 not
supported. The failure, shader_quad_control.terminated_invocation, also fails
with builds from before the wave32 and barycentric work, and with all
TU_EXPERIMENTAL features off, so it is unrelated to this patch.
